WEBVTT

00:00:28.473 --> 00:00:32.339
and by the way, in this talk
when I "energy," I mean "electricity" --

00:00:32.363 --> 00:00:34.323
one thing that's unique about it is

00:00:34.347 --> 00:00:36.929
there isn't much legacy
infrastructure already in place

00:00:36.953 --> 00:00:39.298
in many countries of the region.

00:00:39.322 --> 00:00:42.398
So, for example, according to 2015 data,

00:00:42.422 --> 00:00:45.700
the total installed electricity capacity
in sub-Saharan Africa

00:00:45.724 --> 00:00:48.020
is only about 100 gigawatts.

00:00:48.044 --> 00:00:49.916
That's similar to that of the UK.

00:00:50.615 --> 00:00:53.375
So this actually presents
a unique opportunity

00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:56.629
to build an energy system
in the 21st century

00:00:56.653 --> 00:00:58.050
almost from scratch.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:00.886
The question is: How do you do that?